UncleMario: Good morning, [i]'nak[/i]. [input]I see you've finished moving, ah?
UncleMario: Looking at you stand behind that counter...[pause=1] the memories just comes flooding back.
UncleMario: Your [i]Lola[/i] will definitely be overjoyed to see you now.
UncleMario: Anyway, do you need help with how things are done here? Or are you ready to run this place on your own? (Use mouse wheel or arrow keys to cycle between choices)
- Help me out, Uncle
	UncleMario: [i][wave]Mabuti.[/wave][/i] Listen closely, kid.
	UncleMario: First, get used to looking around. Familiarize yourself with the shelves on your left so you don't take forever looking for things.
	[signal arg="wait_look_at_shelf"]
	UncleMario: Good. Now, your [i]Lola[/i] always said, "you need to know your prices!"
	UncleMario: Press [i]ALT[/i] to toggle your pricing lens. It helps you see how much we're charging.
	[signal arg="wait_for_pricing"]
	UncleMario: There. You can see the item's base and selling price now, as well as the margin percentage. Useful, 'di ba?
	UncleMario: Try using your mouse scroll wheel or the `,` and `.` to adjust the price of that item. 
	UncleMario: Be careful though, as high margins may not sit with other customers. Try to find a balance, ah?
	UncleMario: If you want to earn more, target customers who buy high tier items, as they are more willing to buy those even at a higher margin percentage!
	UncleMario: Now, why don't you try editing the price of Anoba? Don't forget that for every new item!
	UncleMario: I'm actually quite hungry myself! Sell one of those [color=#0f6e2f]Anoba[/color] to me!
	[signal arg="wait_for_pickup"]
	UncleMario: Just drag the item directly onto me to complete the sale.
	[signal arg="wait_for_sale"]
	UncleMario: [wave]Crunch crunch...[/wave] Ahh! That hits the spot. My stomach is satisfied now.
	UncleMario: Now where was I? 
	UncleMario: Ah!
	UncleMario: Over to your right is the Refrigerator. In this heat, people will be dying for a cold soda.
	UncleMario: Go on, try opening it. Just click the handle.
	[signal arg="wait_for_fridge"]
	UncleMario: You can put all sorts of frozen goods here. Do be sure to close it after though, or else the cold will run free!
	UncleMario: Also, there's a trash can nearby to dump extra stock. This is useful for when you buy too much of an item and it's not too popular anymore!
	UncleMario: Sometimes, people will request items that you haven't unlocked yet. Don't be afraid to turn them down, anak.
	UncleMario: As you serve more customers, high tier items will be unlocked in the market. Fill your store with all sorts of products, ah!
	UncleMario: When you buy a new tier, it comes with 2 of each new unlocked items. Keep upgrading your store, anak.
	UncleMario: And if you're running out of stock, just use the phone behind you and dial in my name, [i]"Mario"[/i]!
	UncleMario: Alternatively, you can press the asterisk (*) button as a shortcut. 
	[signal arg="wait_look_at_phone"]
	UncleMario: Oh, and I almost forgot! 
	UncleMario: Some customers would like to loan as well, and if you accept, their names will be put into that notebook near the phone.
	[signal arg="wait_look_at_notebook"]
	jump SuccessOutro
- "[Skip Tutorial] I know the drill."
	jump SkipOutro

label Satisfy
label SuccessOutro
UncleMario: Well, that's all!
UncleMario: I'm going to have my coffee and pandesal now.
jump Outro

label SkipOutro
UncleMario: Right, you've always been a quick one. 
UncleMario: If you're that confident, I'll leave you to it. Just don't burn the place down!
jump Outro

label Outro
UncleMario: Good luck today. Don't work too hard, [i]anak[/i]. See you around!
[signal arg="refuse_service"]